# Overlay example: self-review

Drop this file at `<consumer>/.claude/skills/self-review/SKILL.md.local`.
It is APPENDED to the plugin's SKILL.md at runtime (extend-only — never replaces plugin behavior).

The plugin's generic skill covers the 10-point checklist with generic descriptions of UI (Check #6), i18n (Check #7), and Docs (Check #9). This overlay names the project-specific files and patterns those checks should verify.

---

## <product> user-facing docs mapping (Check #9)

Any change that affects user-facing behavior MUST update both the docs copy AND any embedded copies the project uses (e.g. RAG / chatbot knowledge base):

| What changed | Update these files (BOTH copies if applicable) |
|---|---|
| <Feature A flow> | `docs/<file-A>.md` + `<embedded-path>/<file-A>.md` |
| <Feature B flow> | `docs/<file-B>.md` + `<embedded-path>/<file-B>.md` |
| <Admin flow>     | `docs/<admin-file>.md` |

(Replace these examples with your project's actual user-facing doc paths.)

## <product> UI checks (Check #6)

Beyond the generic "themed wrappers over raw HTML" rule, this project also requires:

- (Project-specific pattern 1 — e.g. "all forms use `<FormProvider>` from react-hook-form")
- (Project-specific pattern 2 — e.g. "modals use the standard `<DialogWithBackdrop>` wrapper, not raw `<Dialog>`")
- (Visual-regression baselines: which directory holds them, and when to update)

## <product> i18n specifics (Check #7)

- Configured locales: read from `project-config.i18n.locales[]` (the bash-guard parity check enforces completeness)
- Translation source-of-truth language: <usually `en`>
- Catalogue location: <e.g. `messages/*.json`>
- Forbidden patterns: hard-coded strings outside the t() helper, English fallback when target locale exists, etc.

## <product> regression test mapping

When fixing a bug in <surface>, the canonical regression-test location is:

- `<surface>` → `__tests__/<surface>.test.ts` + `e2e/<surface>.spec.ts`
- (List the dominant surfaces and their expected test files)
